The authors have upgraded the model from version 3.2 to version 3.3, with significant improvements in the following five areas:
1. N = 1 anchor accuracy. A finite-nuclear-size + QED correction, δ₁ₛ, has been introduced, reducing the maximum error for hydrogen-like ions from +0.364% (U) to within ±0.016%; the error for U⁹⁰⁺ improved from +0.682% to +0.321%.
2. Coverage. A new negative-ion column (N = Z+1) has been added for 78 elements, anchored exactly to experimental electron affinities, extending the grid from 4278 to 4356 points.
3. Uncertainty quantification. The zonal error table has been upgraded to a per-point uncertainty model U(Z, N), calibrated on the full residual set, with a measured coverage of 99.86% (99.25% ± 0.24% in holdout validation), restoring the intended 95% semantics.
4. Full-grid accuracy. The mean absolute relative error improved from 0.260% to 0.254%.
5. Zero cost. All 29 fitted parameters remain frozen, and every published v3.2 statistic is inherited by construction; safeguard corrections decreased from 646 to 640 points, with zero violations in all physical-consistency checks.
